codex
The synthetic last-layer Gaussian approximation is clearly biased at smaller widths; for larger widths it is closer, but still not obviously better. I’ll wait for the default-ish batch to finish before deciding.
codex
The last-layer Gaussian shortcut is not reliable enough. A better targeted correction is full first-layer covariance matching: the first ReLU covariance is known exactly, and matching the whole covariance before layer 2 may improve downstream correlations at modest cost.
